assistant: Subject: Follow next_cursor to return all search results

search_products made one `GET /products?q=…` call and returned only that page. The new vendor version (2026-10-01) splits results into pages: it sent 5 of 7 cable matches with `next_cursor: "5"`, and we never asked for the rest. The v1 API returned all 7 at once with `next_cursor: null`, so this went unnoticed. The handler now keeps requesting `&cursor=<next_cursor>`, using the `cursor` parameter from the published spec, until the cursor is null, then maps the combined items. v1 responses still make a single request and produce the same output, and typecheck, lint and tests pass. One problem is not fixed: the alert also flagged v2 prices that look like cents (6900 for a cable that v1 priced at 69). Nothing in the spec or the response says the unit changed, so I didn't divide by 100 on a guess; this needs confirming with the vendor.

